**Reproduced unresolved teaching shortcut on the current source.** Audited generator SHA-256: `adf97091906a5fabfc39679cfc7494997b79e89c86b88e85355b145d4c8f44c4`; this matches the source hash bound to prior unresolved return `review-d88b3128159c888d:v0001`.

The rival is: **for each complete color-5 frame, project only the first color-7 marker found in top/bottom/left/right scan order.** Canonical frames each have one marker, so this is plausible. A fresh production replay uses seed 0, medium difficulty, and consecutive sample indices 9–12. The first three profiles are `public_2`, `public_3`, `public_2`; the query profile is `cross_stripes`. The rival matches all three live Racket demonstration outputs exactly, while the query has multiple markers and differs on seven cells. All four inputs pass `self_check`; the counterexample is emitted by the unmodified production sampler.

Evidence:

- `checks/audit/a0c6005765ee/inputs.json` and `generation.json` — exact production lesson and source binding;
- `checks/audit/a0c6005765ee/racket.json` — fresh supported Racket labels;
- `checks/audit/a0c6005765ee/report.json` — per-pair fit, exact query input/output/rival, and seven differences;
- `checks/audit/build_reports.py` — independent frame/marker rival reproducer.

Suggested repair in a separate assignment: declare the first-marker rival and schedule at least one multi-marker demonstration in every intended lesson and every permitted query rotation.
